{
  "name": "302. Async task contract: task control fields, cancel route, named key (fork async task contract)",
  "description": "Pins contract C7 (TXE-6521; BF12, BF13) and C3 on the unified video routes. Local fixture regression, no live provider calls: start tests/e2e/api/runners/provider-error-fixture.mjs, start an isolated gateway on tests/e2e/api/provider_config/provider-error-fixture.config.json and run with providerErrorFixture=1; every case is skipped otherwise. openai_video_keys is an OpenAI-shaped provider on the fixture with two keys, video-key-a and video-key-b. The fixture counts every request under /v1/videos by method and bearer token. Rows 2 to 5: each of the four task control fields (callback_url, client_reference_id, expires_after_seconds, output_storage_uri) is refused with 400 caller_unsupported_parameter naming the field, because the provider declares none of them; before the change the field was forwarded or dropped as an extra param and the create succeeded. Row 6: POST /v1/videos/{id}/cancel on a provider with no cancel API is 400 provider_cancel_unsupported; before the change the route did not exist (404 or 405). Rows 7 to 9: a task query with x-bf-api-key uses the named key. Row 10 reads the fixture's counters: two queries with video-key-b, one with video-key-a and nothing else, so the five refused requests made no upstream call and no query used a key other than the one named. A provider that has a cancel API and the cancel-is-delete rule are pinned by the Go tests (core TestVideoCancelRequest, providers/utils TestCancelVideoWhileQueued) until a vendor ticket adds a provider that implements cancel.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "302.1 reset the fixture's hit counters (fork async task contract)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{providerErrorFixtureUrl}}/__reset"
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('the fixture reset its counters', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(200);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().data[0].reset).to.eql(true);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "302.2 [EXPECT-400] openai_video_keys/sora-2 POST /v1/videos refuses the task control field callback_url the provider does not take (fork async task contract)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"model\": \"openai_video_keys/sora-2\",\n  \"prompt\": \"a paper boat on a pond\",\n  \"callback_url\": \"https://hooks.example.test/v/task_1\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/videos",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "videos"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('callback_url is refused as caller_unsupported_parameter naming the field', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(400);",
              "  var j = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(j.extra_fields && j.extra_fields.error_type, 'error_type: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql('caller_unsupported_parameter');",
              "  pm.expect(j.error && j.error.param, 'error.param: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql('callback_url');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
